  "id": "DrugBank_DB00525 - MONDO_5984",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tolnaftate may be associated with Tinea Pedis through a series of indication pathways involving dermatophytosis. Pathway 1 links Tolnaftate to Tinea Barbae, which in turn is associated with Griseofulvin, and Griseofulvin with Tinea Pedis. Pathway 2 and 3 connect Tolnaftate to Dermatophytosis of the groin and perianal area, which is linked to Clioquinol and Naftifine, both of which are also associated with Tinea Pedis. These pathways indicate that Tolnaftate may exert its therapeutic effects through a mechanism involving antifungal activity, potentially targeting the same fungal pathogens that cause Tinea Pedis. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with Path 1 having the highest score, followed by Path 2 and 3. The overlapping pathways highlight the potential for Tolnaftate to be a candidate for repositioning as a treatment for Tinea Pedis, though further clinical validation is needed to confirm its efficacy and safety.",
